{"nodes": [{"id": "readme", "label": "README (The Only Cure)", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "README.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "This version was rebuilt from scratch to support future additions and to feel as close as possible to a vanilla mechanic. Supports Single Player and Multiplayer. Intended to be used with Fancy Handwork and Brutal Handwork mods."}, {"id": "readme_amputation", "label": "Amputation (core mechanic)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "README.md", "source_location": "line 25", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Cut off the infected limb with a Saw/Garden Saw to survive the bite. Bandages/stitches auto-used to raise survival odds; a tourniquet placed on the correct side dampens post-amputation damage. Amputating the upper arm prevents equipping any prosthesis. Player gains skill points for the amputated side, making timed actions faster."}, {"id": "readme_cicatrization", "label": "Cicatrization (wound healing)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "README.md", "source_location": "line 35", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Amputated limbs cicatrize over time; visible in the Health Panel. Wounds should be cleaned with a bandage to help the process. An incompletely cicatrized limb can still take a prosthesis but risks random bleedings."}, {"id": "readme_prosthesis", "label": "Prosthesis (replacement limbs)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "README.md", "source_location": "line 40", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Two types (Hook and Arm) restore missing-hand functionality like two-handed weapons. Hook Prosthesis makes actions take longer but is cheaper to craft; equipping a prosthetic slowly builds familiarity (Prosthesis perk) that speeds actions."}, {"id": 